------------------------------------------------------------
Both shield's looks have been reworked
------------------------------------------------------------
Bulwark’s shield: It is now a gently curved grey plate with a light rim along the front edge. The glass window and the white handle piece are gone.
Ajax’s shield: It is now a smaller, gently curved cyan plate with a bright rim. The glass is removed.
Placed rescue shield: The deployable shield on the ground uses the same curved look, also without glass.
Curve: The bend is mild. It bulges forward by about half a character width on Bulwark and less on Ajax.
------------------------------------------------------------
New squad command system
Command wheel (desktop)

Open: Hold the middle mouse button. A wheel with 8 numbered slices appears in the middle of the screen.
Issue a command: While you hold it, press 1 to 8 to give an order. The slice you used lights up green.
Close: Release the middle button.
While it is open: The number keys send commands instead of switching gear, and you cannot fire.

The 8 commands
Follow me.
Hold position.
Go to aim point.
Stack at door.
Breach and clear.
Hold / free fire: Toggles between holding fire and firing at will.
Regroup: The squad follows you and ceases fire for 3 seconds.
Suppressing fire: New. The squad fires 40% faster for 6 seconds.
------------------------------------------------------------
Landscape view setting (mobile only)

Where: Settings has a new “Landscape view” row, shown only on touch devices.
Effect: With it on, the game rotates to landscape while your phone stays upright, so you can play without turning it. The control buttons float over the sides of the screen.
Controls: It uses the floating on-screen sticks on the game area, as before.
If you turn the phone sideways: The game switches to the normal landscape layout automatically.
Menus: They stay upright even with the setting on.

Other mobile improvements

Vibration: Your phone vibrates briefly when you take a hit.
Auto-pause: The game pauses by itself if you switch apps or tabs.
Zoom: Pinch zoom and double-tap zoom are disabled.
